# rviz_simu_nav2.rviz
# RViz configuration to view the simulation, the TF, the map and the localisation

Fixed Frame: map

Displays:
- Grid
- TF
- RobotModel (base_link)
- LaserScan (/scan, frame_id: laser_link)
- Odometry (/odom, frame_id: base_link)
- Map (/map)
- Pose (/odom, /base_link)

# Instructions :
# 1. Start RViz with: rviz2 -d rviz_simu_nav2.rviz
# 2. Add the topics:
#    - /scan (LaserScan, frame: laser_link)
#    - /odom (Odometry, frame: base_link)
#    - /map (OccupancyGrid, frame: map)
#    - TF (to see every frame)
#    - RobotModel (base_link)
# 3. Check that the odom->base_link TF moves with the robot
# 4. Check that the /odom pose matches the actual position of the robot
# 5. Check that the map grows and does not drift

# Astuce :
# Use "ViewFrames" (ros2 run tf2_tools view_frames) to generate a PDF of the TF tree
# Use "ros2 topic echo /odom" to compare the pose with the simulation
